Axiom 1 (ax2): ldiv(X, op(X, Y)) = Y.
Axiom 2 (ax3): rdiv(op(X, Y), Y) = X.
Axiom 3 (ax4): op(rdiv(X, Y), Y) = X.
Axiom 4 (ax5): op(X, op(X, op(Y, Z))) = op(op(op(X, X), Y), Z).

Lemma 5: rdiv(op(X, op(X, op(Y, Z))), Z) = op(op(X, X), Y).
Proof:
